## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical understanding of basic Azure security controls: private networking, secret management, and policy enforcement in a real-world setup.

## Key Concepts
- Private Endpoints and Storage Account network rules
- Azure Policy to deny public access on storage and require private endpoints
- Key Vault references for secrets in App Settings
- Lightweight rollback and validation in CI/CD

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "connectionStrings": {
    "DefaultConnection": "@Microsoft.KeyVault(SecretUri=https://kv-demo.vault.azure.net/secrets/DbConn/abc)"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollback if private endpoints fail to provision?
- What are the trade-offs of denying public access vs. private endpoints in a multi-region setup?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of basic network security controls in Azure and practical rollout/rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Private Link and Private Endpoints
- Storage Account network rules (default deny)
- Azure Policy enforcement
- Rollback and test strategies

## Code Example
```bicep
param storageAccountName string
param vnetSubnetId string
resource pe 'Microsoft.Network/privateEndpoints@2020-11-01' = {
  name: '${storageAccountName}-pe'
  location: resourceGroup().location
  properties: {
    subnet: { id: vnetSubnetId }
    privateLinkServiceConnections: [
      {
        name: 'storageBlob'
        properties: {
          privateLinkServiceId: '/subscriptions/.../resourceGroups/.../providers/Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/${storageAccountName}'
          groupIds: [ 'blob' ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
        { "not": { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/privateEndpointConnections", "exists": true } }
        }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify the guardrail in CI/CD pipelines?
- How would you extend to multi-region deployments and private DNS considerations?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess storage security, policy enforcement, and rollback capabilities in a practical scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy deny public network access
- Private Endpoints and VNET integration
- Managed Identities RBAC
- Secrets in Key Vault instead of config

## Code Example
```json
{
  "mode": "Indexed",
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "properties.publicNetworkAccess", "equals": "Enabled"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate rollback after applying policy?
- How would you handle temporary public access needs during migrations?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical knowledge of Azure security guardrails using built-in policies, Private Endpoints, and DNS.

## Key Concepts
- Deny public network access policy scope
- Private Endpoints and Private DNS zones
- Exemptions and rollback strategy
- Canary rollout basics

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "anyOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Web/sites"},
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Sql/servers"},
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

